[statement]
A name a real package carries is decided before a name provided only at no
version, whichever a package lists first. `b` lists the virtual `v` first,
but `c` is decided first, and its dependency on `p4` installs a provider of
`v`, so `v` needs nothing more, though `p5` ranks higher for it.

[repository]
P:b
V:1.0-r0
D:v c

P:c
V:1.0-r0
D:p4

P:p4
V:1.0-r0
p:v
k:400

P:p5
V:1.0-r0
p:v
k:500

[request]
b

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install p4 1.0-r0
install c 1.0-r0
install b 1.0-r0
